# Variable names only — no real values. Copy to .env.local and fill in for local development.
# See docs/commerce-architecture.md and docs/deployment.md for what each of these is for.

# --- Commerce: draft-preview mode (optional, local/dev only) ---
# Lets /shop and /shop/[handle] show unpublished draft products when the request includes a
# matching ?preview=<token> query param. Leave unset in production — draft products must never
# be reachable without it. See docs/commerce-architecture.md "Draft-preview mode".
COMMERCE_PREVIEW_TOKEN=

# --- Commerce backend: Supabase (NOT YET CONNECTED — no project exists yet) ---
# Once created: Supabase project settings > API. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are safe to expose to the
# browser (that's what the anon key is for — RLS in supabase/migrations/*.sql is what actually
# restricts it). SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY bypasses RLS entirely — server-only, never prefix it
# with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never log it. See docs/commerce-architecture.md.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Payments: Stripe (NOT YET CONNECTED — no account/keys exist yet) ---
# Test-mode keys from the Stripe Dashboard. STRIPE_SECRET_KEY and STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET are
# server-only. STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET comes from `stripe listen` (local) or the Dashboard's
# webhook endpoint configuration pointed at /api/webhooks/stripe. See
# docs/commerce-architecture.md "Stripe checkout" for the full setup sequence and test cards.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Site URL ---
# Used to build the Stripe Checkout return_url. Defaults to http://localhost:3000 in dev if
# unset — set explicitly for any deployed environment (preview or production).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# --- Deployment (Vercel) ---
# Populated automatically by the Vercel CLI/platform when linked/deployed — not something to
# set by hand. See docs/deployment.md.
# VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN=
